From abe8ac6b6cf20986b3bb877c91d4e879254af8b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:53:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(2d): warn on a selected Helix, Ramp or Plunge
 start-side entry; retire the dead-end ramp

"Pass starts at" Inside or Outside round a part recommends the Arc entry
from the air (#3746). A Helix, Ramp or Plunge that the user selects is
used as selected. Where the Arc entry from the air applies, the ladder
writes one advice note and the operation posts one advisory
Warning::EntryNotRecommended, which names the selected type, Arc and the
reason. The Lead in / Lead out page of 2D Offset keeps every type
selectable and shows the same sentence under the Type selector.

The automatic #3577 dead-end ramp (dead_end_ramp, the ramp_starts marks,
the too_short_at plan check and its fallback note) is removed: the user
did not select it. A later pass that no lead-in reaches takes the pass
link's entry, the user's.

Fixes #3748

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
